==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[præsumptuous]] {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la|en}} {{term|praesumptuosus|lang=la}}. Compare {{term|presumption}}, {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|présomptueux|lang=fr}}, {{etyl|fro|-}} {{term|presumptuous|lang=fro}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/pɹəˈzʌmp.tjuː.əs/}}
* {{IPA|/priˈzəmptʃəs/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Going beyond what is [[right]] or [[proper]] because of an excess of [[self-confidence]] or [[arrogance]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|going beyond what is proper}} [[overconfident]], [[foolhardy]], [[rash]], [[presuming]], [[forward]], [[arrogant]], [[insolent]], [[conceited]]

====Related terms====
* [[presumption]]

